  <title>Pronunciation dictionary</title>
  <p>
    The pronunciation dictionary lets you replace how Orca speaks specific words. Global Voice
    Settings preferences include a switch for whether Orca uses the dictionary; Pronunciation
    preferences are where you add, edit, and remove dictionary entries.
  </p>
  <p>
    For example, replace an abbreviation with its expanded form or use a phonetic spelling for a
    name. Matching is case-insensitive and applies to whole words. Application-specific
    pronunciation entries let you use different replacements in different applications.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-pronunciation-dictionary">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Pronunciation</gui> category.
    </p>
    <p>
      Add a new entry from the dictionary header. Edit or delete an existing entry from its row.
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Add New Pronunciation</gui>: Opens a dialog
          where you can add a word and the replacement text Orca should speak.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Pronunciation Dictionary</gui>: Lists words and
          the replacement text Orca sends to speech before speaking them.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Edit Pronunciation</gui>: Opens a dialog
              where you can change the selected pronunciation entry.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
